course: dictionary
lesson: 5382
title: Context clues: knitting
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You may not know every word, but the words around it can help. Read this sentence: «Liking a quiet hobby like knitting, reading or drawing does not make anyone weird or weak.» Knitting is listed with reading and drawing, and the sentence says it is a hobby, so it must be something quiet that people enjoy doing.
explain: Ask yourself what word would fit. The sentence is about hobbies, and knitting sits in a list of things people like to do. Now try your meaning in the sentence: making things from wool with needles is a quiet hobby, and the sentence still makes sense. That is a good sign your meaning is right.
explain: Knitting can mean the activity, or the thing that is being knitted. Read this: «Her knitting was on the sofa, half-finished.» Here knitting means the item itself, the unfinished piece of work. Look at the words around it to decide which meaning fits.
fact: Knitting means making clothes or other things from wool or yarn by looping it together with two long needles or a machine.
fact: Knitting can also mean the thing being knitted, such as a half-finished scarf.
fact: Knitting is an uncountable noun, so we say some knitting, not a knitting. The verb is knit, knits, knitted or knit, knitting.
fact: Knitting needs patience, and it often means counting rows and stitches, which links to maths patterns.
fact: «Liking a quiet hobby like knitting, reading or drawing does not make anyone weird or weak.»
exercise: «Liking a quiet hobby like knitting, reading or drawing does not make anyone weird or weak.» What does knitting mean? | Running a race in the park | *Making things from wool or yarn by looping it together with needles | Painting pictures on a wall | Cooking food in a hot kitchen
exercise: In «Her knitting was on the sofa, half-finished», what does knitting mean? | *The thing being knitted | Two long needles only | A quiet hobby of reading | Winter weather
exercise: Which of these needs patience and counting rows and stitches? | Running | *Knitting | Jumping | Shouting
test: The sentence says liking knitting «does not make anyone weird or weak». What does this tell you about people who knit? | Loud people always knit | *They are not weird or weak | They must be very old | They never finish anything
test: Mia has a knitting pattern. What is a knitting pattern? | A kind of warm hat | A bag for carrying wool | A song about wool | *Instructions for making a knitted item
exam: In «Knitting keeps my hands busy», what does knitting mean? | *The activity of making things from wool or yarn | Winter weather | Two long needles only | A loud noise
